  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n~\nWork\nTidewater Charts\n\n// Case study\n\nTidewater Charts \n\nA charting layer that pans through a million points without dropping a frame.\n\nVisit the live site\nRead the code\n\nPan and zoom at 1M points\nfrom\n12 fps\n→\nto\n60 fps\n\nClient\nTidewater\nYear\n2023\nRole\nFrontend and WebGL developer\nKind\nExperiment\n01\nThe problem\n\nTidewater's analysts explore sensor data from offshore wind farms. The old SVG charts gave up at around twenty thousand points.\n\n02\nThe approach\nLines and scatter plots draw on the GPU; axes, labels and tooltips stay in the DOM so they remain selectable and readable by a screen reader.\nData is decimated per zoom level in a worker, with the raw points fetched only when the user gets close.\nEvery chart has a table view with the same data, one key press away.\nTwo developers working late on laptops, city lights outside\nPhone wireframe sketches on paper and a hand with a pen\n03\nThe result\n\nA million points pan at a steady 60 frames a second on a three year old laptop. Analysts stopped exporting to spreadsheets to look at a week of data.\n\nBuilt with\n\nTypeScript\nWebGL\nregl\nWeb Workers\n\nNext case\nTooling · 2023\nHalden Design System\nSixty-two components, one token file and no accessibility exceptions.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n17:01 CEST\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.\n\nEdit Content",
